  m_Name: hymenoptera
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::WordInfo
  words:
  - hymenoptera
  info: "Hymenoptera is an order of insects with over 150,000 described species;
    its most well known species include ants, bees, and wasps. Ants and some species
    of bees and wasps are some of the most well known social insects, as they live
    in colonies or hives with many of their kin. They are often identifiable by their
    narrow waists that separates their thorax and abdomen. \n\nSource: https://www.britannica.com/animal/hymenopteran "
  image: {fileID: 2800000, guid: cf74d920fdba01c47a86eeed7544a74b, type: 3}
